dzn: Copy 8-bit textures through a buffer on Intel

Intel's Direct3D 12 driver copies textures of 8-bit formats with
CopyTextureRegion into the wrong texels: a UHD 770 under WSL2 failed every
dEQP-GLES31 copy_image.non_compressed case of the R8 formats (312), and
passed the others. Dawn works around the same bug for formats under 4 bytes
on older Intel GPUs (Gen9 and Gen9.5) by copying through a buffer.

On Intel, a copy between single-sampled color images of an 8-bit format
goes through Dozen's staging buffer, as copies between incompatible formats
already do.

